Curated fuzz seeds (design §50.3).

Every file here is hand-written and explainable: a real protocol sample, or a
specific attack the design names — CL/TE conflict, duplicate Content-Length,
obs-fold, CRLF injection, an over-large port, a decompression bomb — or a
regression input for a bug that was actually found.

Soak-grown corpora are deliberately NOT committed. A 45-second run per target
grew this to ~29,000 files and 47 MB, and even after `-merge=1` minimisation it
was 11,914 files and 47 MB of unexplainable blobs. Those belong in CI
artifacts, which is what the `soak` job in .github/workflows/fuzz.yaml
uploads. What lives in git is the part a reviewer can read.

Naming: `seedNN` for the enumerated cases, otherwise a name saying what the
input is. `regress-*` marks an input that once crashed something.
